! ========================================================================
! SLICE INPUT CONFIGURATION FILE
! ========================================================================
! This file defines the slices of the computational domain to be saved
! during processing. Each slice is defined by its direction and index.
!
! DIRECTIONS:
!   X - slice perpendicular to X-axis (YZ plane)
!   Y - slice perpendicular to Y-axis (XZ plane) 
!   Z - slice perpendicular to Z-axis (XY plane)
!
! INDEX: Grid point index in the specified direction (1-based indexing)
!
! FORMAT: Each slice is defined on a separate line as:
!   DIRECTION  INDEX
!
! NOTES:
! - Lines starting with '!' are comments and will be ignored
! - Empty lines are ignored
! - Index must be within the valid range for your grid
! - Maximum number of slices is limited by available memory
! ========================================================================

! Number of slices to save
2                               ! NSLICES - total number of slices

! Slice definitions (DIRECTION INDEX)
X    512                          ! X-slice at index 1 (YZ plane)
Y    256                        ! Y-slice at index 256 (XZ plane)
Z    0                        ! Z-slice at index 257 (XY plane)

! ========================================================================
! ADDITIONAL EXAMPLES (commented out):
! Y    96                       ! Y-slice at index 96
! Z    80                       ! Z-slice at index 80
! X   192                       ! X-slice at index 192
! ========================================================================